{"id":1049185,"date":"2026-09-22T09:38:53","date_gmt":"2026-09-22T13:38:53","guid":{"rendered":"https://www.nasa.gov/?p=1049185"},"modified":"2026-09-22T13:14:03","modified_gmt":"2026-09-22T17:14:03","slug":"nasa-astronaut-to-answer-questions-from-new-hampshire-students","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https://www.nasa.gov/learning-resources/nasa-astronaut-to-answer-questions-from-new-hampshire-students/","title":{"rendered":"NASA Astronaut to Answer Questions from New Hampshire Students"},"content":{"rendered":"<div id=\"\" class=\"padding-top-5 padding-bottom-3 width-full maxw-full hds-module hds-module-full alignfull wp-block-nasa-blocks-article-intro\"><div class=\"width-full maxw-full article-header\"><div class=\"margin-bottom-2 width-full maxw-full\"><p class=\"label carbon-60 margin-0 margin-bottom-3 padding-0\">2 min read</p><h1 class=\"display-48 margin-bottom-2\">NASA Astronaut to Answer Questions from New Hampshire Students</h1></div></div></div>\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"hds-media hds-module wp-block-image\"><div class=\"margin-left-auto margin-right-auto nasa-block-align-inline\"><div class=\"hds-media-wrapper margin-left-auto margin-right-auto\"><figure class=\"hds-media-inner hds-cover-wrapper hds-media-ratio-none \"><a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg\"><img decoding=\"async\" width=\"1280\" height=\"1920\" src=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?w=1280\" class=\"attachment-2048x2048 size-2048x2048\" alt=\"NASA astronaut Anil Menon reviews procedures for emergency scenarios while aboard the International Space Station as part of his long-duration science and research mission.\" style=\"transform: scale(1); transform-origin: 50% 50%; object-position: 50% 50%; object-fit: cover;\" block_context=\"nasa-block\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg 1280w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=200,300 200w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=768,1152 768w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=683,1024 683w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=1024,1536 1024w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=267,400 267w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=400,600 400w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=600,900 600w, https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/anil-menon-downlink-sept-22.jpg?resize=800,1200 800w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1280px) 100vw, 1280px\" /></a></figure><figcaption class=\"hds-caption padding-y-2\"><div class=\"hds-caption-text p-sm margin-0\">NASA astronaut Anil Menon reviews procedures for emergency scenarios while aboard the International Space Station as part of his long-duration science and research mission.</div><div class=\"hds-credits\">Credit: NASA</div></figcaption></div></div></div>\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><em><strong>Editor’s Note: This feature was updated Sept. 22, 2026, to note the time change for the in-flight call with students. </strong></em></p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Students in New Hampshire will hear from NASA astronaut Anil Menon as he answers prerecorded STEM questions while aboard the&nbsp;<a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/international-space-station/\">International Space Station</a>.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">The Earth-to-space call will begin at 11:40 a.m. EDT Thursday, Sept. 24, and will stream live on the agency’s Learn With NASA <a href=\"https://youtube.com/live/gvo7ReEOeXE\" rel=\"noopener\">YouTube</a> channel.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">This event is hosted by the McAuliffe-Shepard Discovery Center in Concord, New Hampshire, for students in grades K-12, and members of the community. This unique opportunity aims to deepen understanding of space exploration and enhance awareness of STEM careers.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Media interested in covering the event must RSVP no later than 5 p.m. EDT, Wednesday, Sept. 23, to Kelly Thompson at kthompson@starhop.com.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For more than 25 years, people have lived and worked continuously aboard the International Space Station, advancing scientific knowledge and making research breakthroughs not possible on Earth. The space station helps NASA understand and overcome the challenges of human spaceflight, expand commercial opportunities in low Earth orbit, and build on the foundation for long-duration missions to the Moon, as part of the Artemis program, and to Mars.</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">For more information on NASA in-flight calls, visit:</p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-text-align-center wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://www.nasa.gov/stemonstation\"><strong>https://www.nasa.gov/stemonstation</strong></a></p>\n\n\n<div id=\"\" class=\"nasa-gb-align-full width-full maxw-full padding-x-3 padding-y-0 nasa_template_article_a hds-module hds-module-full alignfull wp-block-nasa-blocks-credits-and-details\">\n<section class=\"padding-x-0 padding-top-5 padding-bottom-2 desktop:padding-top-7 desktop:padding-bottom-9\">\n\t<div class=\"grid-row grid-container maxw-widescreen padding-0\">\n\t\t<div class=\"grid-col-12 desktop:grid-col-2 padding-right-4 margin-bottom-5 desktop:margin-bottom-0\">\n\t\t\t<div class=\"padding-top-3 border-top-1px border-color-carbon-black\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"margin-bottom-2\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"heading-14\">Share</h2>\n\t\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"padding-bottom-2\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<ul class=\"social-icons social-icons-round\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t<li class=\"social-icon social-icon-x\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<a href=\"h